component SigilCompilationReportProtocol {
  goal {
    Own compiler diagnostic identity, report schema, proposal-report identity,
    trace schema, staleness, and diagnostic lifecycle comparison.
  }

  interface {
    CompilationDiagnostic {
      every error and warning has a stable rule code, diagnostic fingerprint,
      originating stage and skill, primary location, evidence, impact, correction
      guidance, evaluator provenance, and zero or more compiler-verified semantic
      subjects
    }

    DiagnosticSemanticSubject {
      relation is direct, governing, or related

      subject identity contains governing Sigil path, component, owner, section,
      optional concept, and optional normalized semantic-unit fingerprint
    }

    CompilationReport {
      version 2 is the authoritative durable result and binds status to source
      hashes, component graph, effective profile, stages, evaluator environment, and
      completed passes

      currentDiagnostics contains current CompilationDiagnostic values whose
      lifecycle is new, unchanged, or regressed; resolvedDiagnostics contains
      retained ResolvedCompilationDiagnostic values

      terminal, Markdown, CI, and editor views are projections of this report
    }

    ResolvedCompilationDiagnostic {
      lifecycle is resolved and retained fields are stable diagnostic identity, prior
      severity, primary location, semantic subjects, first-seen run, and last-active
      run
    }

    CompilationProposalReport {
      a proposal report identifies session, baseEpoch, generation, base fingerprint,
      proposed paths, and proposal fingerprint without proposed contents or temporary
      paths
    }

    EvaluationTrace {
      records requested stages, command events, usage, evaluator environment, and
      incomplete evidence without hidden reasoning or complete file contents
    }

    ReportConstruction {
      constructReport(evaluationIdentity, currentDiagnostics, status,
      EvaluationTrace, evaluatorOutcomes, priorReport?, proposalIdentity?) validates
      matching source, target, profile, stage, evaluator, and optional proposal
      identities and returns one authoritative CompilationReport

      invalid or inconsistent internal construction input rejects with
      COMPILER_FAILED and returns no partial report
    }
  }
}

expand SigilCompilationReportProtocol {
  state {
    DiagnosticLifecycle {
      A current diagnostic is new, unchanged, or regressed relative to the selected
      prior report. A prior active diagnostic absent from the current evaluation is
      retained as resolved.
    }
  }

  logic {
    CompilationDiagnostic {
      Derive diagnostic identity from stable rule, stage, subject, and
      source-location facts rather than evaluator prose.

      Resolve every evaluator-provided Sigil location against the deterministic
      semantic model and attach the smallest containing semantic unit, falling back
      to its containing concept or section when no semantic unit contains the
      location.

      Resolve an implementation location through validated ownership annotations and
      attach every governing component or concept section selected by the owning
      implementation entrypoint.

      Preserve the physical primary location separately from its semantic subjects.

      Derive semantic-unit fingerprints from normalized prose and literal content so
      canonical formatting and physical line movement do not change semantic
      identity.

      Reject or reduce unsupported evaluator claims to information so they cannot
      make compilation red or yellow.

      Classify a current stable identity as unchanged when it was active in the prior
      report, including when its current severity differs. Store the current severity
      and let status calculation use current evidence.

      Classify a current stable identity as regressed when the prior report retained
      it as resolved, and as new when neither prior active nor resolved diagnostics
      contain it.

      Classify a prior active identity as resolved when current evaluation does not
      contain it. Place it only in resolvedDiagnostics with its retained identity,
      prior severity and location, semantic subjects, first-seen run, and last-active
      run; resolved entries do not affect current status.
    }

    ReportConstruction {
      Apply CompilationDiagnostic identity and DiagnosticLifecycle rules to current
      diagnostics and the optional compatible prior report, then bind the supplied
      status, EvaluationTrace, evaluator outcomes, and optional proposal identity to
      the same validated evaluation identity.

      Construct the complete version-2 report before returning it. Never expose a
      mutable builder or partially validated report.
    }

  }

  constraints {
    CompilationReport {
      CompilationReport version 2 requires semanticSubjects on every diagnostic,
      including an empty array when deterministic resolution finds no governing Sigil
      subject.

      Direct report consumers accept exactly version 2. An older or unknown report
      version rejects with COMPILER_FAILED before field interpretation, and no report
      migration is provided. Optional evidence stores may instead decline an
      incompatible report under their own lookup contract.

      Semantic subject identities are compiler-owned projections; evaluator text may
      provide candidate physical locations but cannot assign a component, section,
      concept, relation, or semantic-unit fingerprint.

      A direct subject contains the primary Sigil location, a governing subject is
      derived from implementation ownership, and a related subject identifies
      additional Sigil evidence for the same finding.

      CompilationReport excludes credentials, hidden reasoning, and complete private
      prompts.

      Proposal reports and traces may include proposed paths, generation numbers,
      base fingerprints, and proposal fingerprints, but never proposed source
      contents or temporary filesystem paths.

      A stage-scoped report identifies the requested stage and exact executed
      dependency closure.

      ReportConstruction rejects mismatched source, target, profile, stage,
      evaluator, trace, status, or proposal identity with COMPILER_FAILED and exposes
      no partial CompilationReport.
    }
  }

  decisions {
    SemanticDiagnosticSubjects {
      Decision: Add compiler-verified hierarchical semantic subjects to every
      diagnostic and make them required in CompilationReport version 2.

      Scope: Governs diagnostic navigation, grouping, lifecycle identity, editor
      integration, implementation reconciliation, and durable report compatibility.

      Assumptions: SigilCore preserves semantic-unit ownership, section, optional
      concept identity, normalized prose, literal content, and exact source range.

      Trade-offs: Report consumers must migrate to version 2 and implementation
      locations require valid ownership annotations before they can gain governing
      semantic subjects.

      Design issues addressed: A physical file and line cannot reliably group a
      finding by component, section, concept, or semantic occurrence and changes when
      formatting moves source lines.

      Discarded alternatives: A single concept-only annotation, evaluator-assigned
      semantic identities, and optional version-1 subject hints were rejected because
      they lose ungrouped units, weaken trust, or leave consumers with an ambiguous
      compatibility contract.

      Consequences: Reports can navigate and group findings at every semantic level,
      and diagnostic identity remains stable across formatting-only changes.

      Revisit when: Sigil introduces explicit durable identifiers for individual
      semantic units.
    }

    DiagnosticLifecycleComparison {
      Decision: Compare current diagnostic identities with both active and retained
      resolved identities from one selected prior report.

      Scope: Governs new, unchanged, regressed, and resolved report representation;
      excludes prior-report storage selection and compilation-status policy.

      Trade-offs: Reports retain bounded identity metadata for resolved diagnostics.

      Design issues addressed: Recurrence after resolution must differ observably
      from a diagnostic first seen in the current run.

      Consequences: Severity changes use current evidence without changing lifecycle,
      while resolved findings remain visible but do not affect current status.
    }

    ReportVersionCompatibility {
      Decision: Accept CompilationReport version 2 without migration and reject other
      versions before interpreting their fields.

      Scope: Governs direct report compatibility; permits optional evidence stores to
      treat incompatible history as absent under their own contract.

      Trade-offs: Consumers must upgrade explicitly instead of relying on implicit
      migration.

      Discarded alternatives: Best-effort interpretation and automatic migration were
      rejected because they could misread authoritative diagnostic identity.

      Consequences: Direct consumers fail predictably with COMPILER_FAILED, while
      incompatible cache evidence remains safely optional.
    }

  }

  cases {
    CompilationReport {
      Changing relevant Sigil content or the effective profile makes an exported
      green report stale.

      A diagnostic located in a grouped interface paragraph identifies its component,
      interface section, concept, exact semantic unit, and direct relation.

      A diagnostic located on an implementation entrypoint with two valid ownership
      targets contains two governing semantic subjects.

      A diagnostic outside Sigil with no valid ownership target contains an empty
      semanticSubjects array while preserving its physical primary location.

      Reformatting a semantic unit without changing its normalized prose or literal
      content preserves its semantic-unit fingerprint.

      A current identity absent from prior active and resolved diagnostics is new. A
      prior active identity seen again is unchanged even when severity changes, and
      the current severity controls status.

      A prior active identity absent from current evaluation moves to
      resolvedDiagnostics and no longer affects status. Its later recurrence is
      regressed rather than new.

      Direct consumption of version 1 or an unknown report version rejects with
      COMPILER_FAILED before interpreting report fields; optional history lookup may
      return no prior evidence instead.

      Consistent evaluation, status, trace, evaluator, prior-report, and optional
      proposal inputs construct one complete authoritative version-2 report.

      Any mismatched construction identity rejects with COMPILER_FAILED and exposes
      no partial report.

      A green report handed to an implementation team still requires human approval
      before implementation begins.

      Successful and failed proposal evaluation may report permitted identifiers but
      never proposed source contents or temporary filesystem paths.

      Failed create, apply, close, and cleanup traces redact proposed contents and
      temporary paths while retaining stable failure codes.

    }
  }
}
